menu "Storage"

choice STORAGE_BACKEND
    prompt "Storage backend"
    default STORAGE_BACKEND_RAM
    help
        Selects the persistence backend behind the key_store / intent_log
        seam. The Application Module talks ONLY to the interfaces in
        key_store.h and intent_log.h — swapping the backend must never change
        an application call site.

        RAM is the provisional placeholder: it keeps the authorized-key list
        and intent target in RAM only, exactly like the original nvs_store.c
        array. It is honest about having no power-loss persistence.

        The NVS backend and the secure-element + RAM + write-policy design
        are planned and will be added to this choice when they land.

    config STORAGE_BACKEND_RAM
        bool "RAM placeholder (no persistence)"

    # Planned — added with the NVS backend implementation:
    # config STORAGE_BACKEND_NVS
    #     bool "NVS flash backend"

    # Planned — added with the secure-element + write-policy design:
    # config STORAGE_BACKEND_SECURE_ELEMENT
    #     bool "Secure element backend"

endchoice

endmenu
